<GuideLayout title="Intermediate 3.6 · Blood Moon Rises & Graduation" current="intermediate">
  <div class="page-grid">
    <aside class="sidebar"><IntermediateNav current="3-6" /></aside>
    <article class="content">
      <header class="chapter-header">
        <div class="chapter-kicker">Intermediate · Chapter 3.6 · the final quest</div>
        <h1 class="chapter-title">Blood Moon Rises &amp; Graduation</h1>
        <p class="chapter-summary">Use the quest XP you have earned to finish the skills for The Blood Moon Rises, complete the Myreque story, and claim your Quest Cape. After that, choose your next adventure.</p>
      </header>
      <ChapterGoals
        summary="Finish Woodcutting, Smithing, Cooking and Fletching → The Blood Moon Rises → all-green quest journal → Quest Cape."
        stats={["74 Woodcutting without a boost", "72 Smithing and Cooking without boosts", "70 Fletching without a boost; earlier chapters covered the other six requirements"]}
        unlocks={["Vampyrium, Hallowed flail and Sunspear", "Quest point cape and hood after every released quest is green", "No mandatory Bowfa, Slayer-unique, raid or post-quest boss farm"]}
      />
      <div class="callout"><strong>Check your levels after the quest rewards.</strong> Dragon Slayer II awarded 80,000 Smithing XP and Grim Tales awarded 60,000 Woodcutting XP; you may also have used the Curse of the Empty Lord museum lamp on Fletching. These rewards have already increased the XP shown in your skill tab. Check it before gathering more materials. Keep your 74+ Slayer, 75+ Magic/Ranged, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, Piety and familiar quest and travel equipment ready.</div>

      <section><div class="section-label">Final training · four skills to check</div><h2>Finish the levels needed for The Blood Moon Rises.</h2>
        <p>Check each skill below and skip any training whose target you have already reached. Otherwise, subtract your current XP from the listed total to find how much remains. The Blood Moon Rises requires all four levels without boosts.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Woodcutting 74:</strong> <strong>1,096,278 XP</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Smithing 72:</strong> <strong>899,257 XP</strong>; check after receiving DS2's 80,000 XP.</li>
          <li><strong>Cooking 72:</strong> <strong>899,257 XP</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Fletching 70:</strong> <strong>737,627 XP</strong>; use the museum lamp first if you chose Fletching.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <RouteStep id="i36-woodcutting" number="1" title="Reach 74 Woodcutting for The Blood Moon Rises">
        <p>Check your Woodcutting XP after the training for Grim Tales' 71-Woodcutting requirement and its <strong>60,000-XP reward</strong>. Return to <strong>Sulliusceps</strong> on Fossil Island if you enjoyed them in Chapter 1, keeping useful fossils and caps along the way. For a calmer session, cut Forestry trees, teaks, maples or yews near convenient transport and a bank. Use ordinary chopping, or a faster method you enjoy. <strong>Stop at an unboosted 74</strong>; extra levels and cap drops are optional.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-smithing" number="2" title="Finish 72 Smithing after Dragon Slayer II's reward">
        <p>Check your Smithing level after receiving DS2's reward. If below 72, use <strong>Giants' Foundry</strong> to turn spare banked metal into Smithing XP and coins, or smith spare bars at an anvil if you prefer. Keep the bars needed for ammunition, quests and Sailing. <strong>Stop at an unboosted 72.</strong> If you already reached 73 to make adamant bolts in 3.3, you can skip this training.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-cooking" number="3" title="Reach 72 Cooking and bank food for bosses">
        <p>Cook banked raw fish or karambwans at a convenient range. If you need more, catch karambwans or other useful fish so the training also leaves you food for bosses. Check your current XP before deciding how much to catch. Cook normally and <strong>stop at an unboosted 72</strong>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-fletching" number="4" title="Reach 70 Fletching with your banked materials">
        <p>Check your Fletching XP after earlier quest rewards, Devious Minds, any bolts you made and the <strong>10,000-XP Curse of the Empty Lord museum lamp</strong> if you chose Fletching. Make <strong>unstrung bows from banked maple, yew or other suitable logs</strong>. Use kingdom maples if you have them. Banked unfinished bows, shafts, feathers or spare bars/darts are alternatives; keep the ammunition you need for combat.</p>
        <p>If <strong>Broader Fletching</strong> is unlocked, broad arrows offer faster training at a higher material cost. Otherwise, decide whether its permanent unlock is worth <strong>300 Slayer points</strong> to you; making bows lets you keep those points. <strong>Stop at an unboosted 70.</strong></p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Blood Moon Rises · requirements and supplies</div><h2>Check your skills, then pack for the opening fight.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i36-preflight" number="5" title="Check The Blood Moon Rises' requirements and prepare your inventory">
        <p>Check for <strong>74 Slayer, 74 Woodcutting, 72 Smithing, 72 Cooking, 70 Fletching, 66 Mining, 65 Hunter, 64 Crafting, 64 Herblore and 57 Magic</strong>. All ten must be reached <strong>without boosts</strong>. Earlier chapters covered Slayer, Mining, Hunter, Crafting, Herblore and Magic; the training above finishes Woodcutting, Smithing, Cooking and Fletching. Confirm <strong>Sins of the Father</strong> and <strong>A Night at the Theatre</strong> are green in your quest journal. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Blood_Moon_Rises" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest requirements and phase guide</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Recover missing equipment and prepare for the opening fight" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Bring your <strong>blisterwood flail and complete Vyre noble outfit</strong>. Reuse the flail from A Night at the Theatre, or buy a <strong>40,000-coin replacement from Ivan</strong> if it is missing. The chest beside him supplies the noble clothes for free. Recover a missing <strong>Drakan's medallion</strong> using the <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-2-5/#i25-sins`}>post-Sins replacement source</a> for convenient travel. During the quest, <strong>Old Man Ral just outside the hideout</strong> can also replace the flail when that option becomes available.</p>
          <p>Pack the Chapter 3.3 crossbow and some remaining ammunition for the opening <strong>acidic bloodvelds</strong>. A faster ranged switch is useful if you prefer one: after the already-completed Tourist Trap, smith <strong>two iron bars into 20 iron dart tips</strong> and add <strong>20 feathers</strong> for a small starter stack. Mine/smelt iron ore until the two bars are ready and buy feathers from Gerrant if missing; you already meet the 19 Smithing and 22 Fletching needed for the darts. Replace the ammunition you use before another attempt.</p>
          <p>Make missing <a href={`${base}intermediate/chapter-1-4/#i14-potion-supplies`}>Prayer potions and ordinary energy/stat-restoration supplies</a> before the initial fight. Rebank at the story's supply points. Inside Vampyrium, collect fresh local food/potions from the named crates and tables; they are renewable quest supplies and cannot be banked for other activities.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>Prepare the <strong>Blisterwood flail</strong>, Drakan's medallion, Vyre noble clothes, ordinary melee/defensive armour, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, dragon defender, <strong>a Ranged weapon with ammunition for the opening acidic bloodvelds</strong>, food, Prayer restores, run energy and an exit/travel plan. The flail is retained from Sins of the Father; if it is missing, take <strong>40,000 coins</strong> to buy a replacement from Ivan at the Meiyerditch Myreque hideout. Noble clothes can be recovered free from its chest. Pack a tinderbox and pickaxe if convenient; the quest can supply those, plus the later hammer, knife, chisel and blisterwood logs. Re-bank by phase rather than carrying every tool at once. No rare weapon or boss unique is an entry condition.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-early-story" number="6" title="Start with Sarius, reach Vampyrium and survive the Blood Hunt">
        <p>Travel to the <strong>Icyene Graveyard</strong> (boat from southern Burgh de Rott or Meiyerditch, or approach from Slepe) and speak to <strong>Sarius Guile</strong>. Regroup with Ivan at the hideout beneath Old Man Ral's house. Wear the Vyre noble clothes for the opening infiltration and defend Ivan: use Protect from Melee, tag attackers off him, prioritise the Vyrewatch Sentinels and <strong>shoot approaching acidic bloodvelds with the Ranged switch</strong>. The quest then moves through <strong>Paterdomus, a portal into Vampyrium, Castle Drakan's key/clock puzzles and haemalchemic stockpile</strong>. Follow Quest Helper or the linked quest guide for exact puzzle clicks; keep inventory space and bank when the story returns you to a supply point.</p>
        <p>The <strong>first Drakan encounter</strong> is movement and reaction practice, not a DPS test. Begin with Protect from Melee. His blood marks collect on the side he will swipe; early sparkles show the opposite safe tiles. Move only as his red glow/sound cue commits the lunge, leave a tile behind you, and attack after a successful dodge. Later fights remove the sparkles and add cleaves, waves and blood magic. Quick-escape/resupply if necessary. During the <strong>Blood Hunt</strong>, repair the Sangvesti drawbridge, move between ruins without letting Drakan catch you, fight the feral vyres and Nylocas using the quest's nearby supplies/throwable spines, then escape through the forest and river. Practise the attack signals and movement with your existing equipment.</p>
        <div class="callout"><strong>Vampyrium supply primer.</strong> The quest's renewable local consumables are for its Vampyrium sections and cannot be banked: <strong>mysterious jerky</strong> is substantial food; <strong>smelly kebabs</strong> are fast food; <strong>foul chunky potions</strong> restore stats/Prayer and add Prayer regeneration; <strong>putrid sticky potions</strong> restore run like stamina; <strong>rank frothy potions</strong> are super-combat boosts; <strong>rancid slimy potions</strong> heal like brews with a small stat drain; and a <strong>jar of congealed blood</strong> fully restores HP and Prayer. Check supply crates/tables at each checkpoint. You do not need to bankroll endless outside brews for these fights.</div>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-flail" number="7" title="Make the Hallowed flail during Hallowed Preparations">
        <p>At Efaritay's palace, finish the short preparation tasks, then <strong>free seven inventory spaces</strong>. Take the workbench tools, blisterwood logs and blessed silver sickle from the room's crates, and the diamond plus enchant-diamond tablet from its chests. Use the diamond and tablet on the sickle, the logs on the sickle, then use the enchanted blisterwood sickle at the anvil to upgrade your Blisterwood flail into the <strong>Hallowed flail</strong>. Make the required five blisterwood stakes from the supplied logs for the next part of the quest. All materials for the upgrade are available in the room.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Use the room's supplies for the upgrade" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>The <strong>blessed silver sickle, blisterwood logs, diamond, enchant-diamond tablet and workbench tools</strong> are supplied in Efaritay's preparation room. Keep <strong>seven free spaces</strong> before collecting them. Use the room's diamond/tablet for the flail upgrade; do not consume a banked diamond reserved for ammunition or hunt another one outside the quest. Make the <strong>five stakes</strong> from the supplied logs as directed, and keep the Hallowed flail for the following fights.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
        <p>The Hallowed flail is <strong>one-handed</strong>, so use the dragon defender with it. Keep Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, Piety and your best sensible melee/defensive armour around that weapon for Drakan. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Hallowed_flail" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Weapon and creation details</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-theatre-wyrd" number="8" title="Finish the Theatre return and Wyrd before the final siege">
        <p>After the palace defence begins, the story returns to Gielinor for <strong>Another Night at the Theatre</strong>. You already learned Entry Mode in 3.4. Bank/regear at Burgh de Rott or Ver Sinhaza: bring ordinary melee, your crossbow, a Magic attack, food and restores. In the quest's Nylocas waves, match <strong>white/melee, green/ranged, blue/magic</strong> and prioritise dangerous blue targets. Range the <strong>Maiden of Sugadinti</strong> from the south; kill her healing Nylocas at the HP breaks and step off blood pools. The <strong>Nylocas Vasilias</strong> changes colour and attack style: switch protection first, then answer with the matching damage style. Your existing gear works for these quest encounters. <strong>Unlike the Vampyrium instances, deaths in this Theatre segment are normal gravestone deaths with possible reclaim fees</strong>; bank a medallion or other return transport and retrieve promptly.</p>
        <p>Next, bank at Burgh de Rott and enter the ruined building north-east of town for <strong>Wyrd</strong>. In melee, Protect from Melee reduces his pushing hits. His repeated cycle has two melee hits, a screech, two hits, another screech and a side-dependent double slam; <strong>turn the overhead off for a screech</strong> and move opposite the arm/side signalled for the slams. At lower HP a bloody screech fills the arena with pools: run out through the opening, keep prayer off until the blast clears, and accept a little pool damage rather than standing in the burst. Ranging from afar avoids his specials but takes unblocked Magic hits; it is an option, not a required weapon swap. Wyrd death returns you outside the lab with items intact, near the Burgh bank. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Blood_Moon_Rises" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Theatre and Wyrd mechanics</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-siege" number="9" title="Hold Drakan's Siege and complete the later story encounter">
        <p>Back at Efaritay's palace, take the <strong>silvthrill ballista and javelins</strong> dropped on the bridge and shoot incoming blood portals. Keep shooting until the defence advances. Inside, help the aranei recover from falling rubble and respond to cracks in the windows/pillars to keep the hideout standing. Refill from the local supply table before <strong>Drakan's next combat round</strong>. Use the Hallowed flail, Protect from Melee and Piety, and react to the expanded spear/AoE patterns instead of forcing extra hits. Efaritay helps with healing, but you still need to dodge. After the siege, the story returns to Darkmeyer for another assisted Drakan encounter; keep room to step back, dodge the three-swipe sequences and the follow-up orb, and refill before the true final battle. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Blood_Moon_Rises" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Siege and later encounter</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">Final boss · Lowerniel Drakan</div><h2>Watch the attack, dodge, then strike.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i36-drakan" number="10" title="Defeat final Drakan and complete The Blood Moon Rises">
        <p>Follow Efaritay through the graveyard portal back to Vampyrium. At the supply chest by the rooftop door, use the <strong>Hallowed flail + dragon defender, Fire Cape, Barrows gloves, best reasonable melee armour, Protect from Melee and Piety</strong>. Bring a <strong>jar of congealed blood</strong> (one per inventory) as a true emergency full HP/Prayer restore. Fill the rest with local rancid slimy healing, several foul chunky Prayer/stat restores and rank frothy combat boosts; jerky/kebabs are useful simpler food. Putrid sticky stamina is for travel, not this stationary final fight. Refill at the chest between attempts. No Slayer helmet, whip, Bowfa, blowpipe or raid weapon is assumed.</p>
        <p><strong>Phase 1 — swipe and lunge recognition:</strong> watch the side that absorbs his blood marks and move to the opposite safe side when his red cue commits. His spear combos grow from side swipes into slam and front/back or semicircle cleaves; keep a few free tiles behind you and reposition around a corner if a wall removes your dodge. Protect from Melee reduces chip damage, not every special. Dodge first, then attack during the opening.</p>
        <p><strong>Phase 2 — blood waves and Magic:</strong> when he disappears and the roof floods, face the incoming walls and <strong>run straight through each wave toward it</strong>; diagonal or spam-clicked pathing often fails. After the final wave, Drakan reappears and fires a cluster of red blood projectiles: activate <strong>Protect from Magic before impact</strong>, then return to Melee protection for his approach/combo. Later single red Magic projectiles need the same brief switch. Dodge, attack during the opening, then reset your positioning.</p>
        <p><strong>Phase 3 — pools, lightning and lunges:</strong> avoid blood pools and the lightning's dark floor shadows, both of which can disable your overhead. When Drakan appears to line up the spear lunge, move a few tiles <strong>perpendicular/out of its footprint</strong>, not across the length of his attack. After the lunge sequence, block the returning red projectile cluster with Protect from Magic and resume Melee protection for the combo. The signals speed up across phases. Use one heal or potion between reads, save the jar for a real emergency, and use each attempt to learn the signals and movement. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/The_Blood_Moon_Rises" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Full current Drakan fight reference</a>.</p>
        <p><strong>Retry costs:</strong> in the Vampyrium quest instances, a normal account/standard Ironman who dies keeps their items, respawns near a checkpoint or supply area and pays no ordinary death fee; the final fight returns you to its door with HP/Prayer restored and its supply chest available, but restarts at phase 1. Teleporting away requires returning through the Icyene Graveyard portal. <strong>Hardcore Ironmen still lose status on death.</strong> This does not override the Theatre segment's ordinary gravestone rules above. Learn the missed mechanic, refill, and retry.</p>
        <p>Claim <strong>4 Quest Points, Vampyrium access, the Hallowed flail and Sunspear, Maggot King access, new Vampyrium skilling/Slayer options and the restored Burgh de Rott pub</strong>. Returning to fight the Maggot King for uniques is optional. The reward <strong>tome of experience has six uses of 30,000 XP</strong> on an eligible skill at <em>level 70 or above</em>. You can choose the same skill repeatedly or save the tome and reclaim it from Efaritay at Castle Drakan. Use it for whichever goal you want to pursue after the Quest Cape.</p>
      </RouteStep>

      <section><div class="section-label">The final journal check</div><h2>Make sure every released quest is complete.</h2></section>
      <RouteStep id="i36-journal" number="11" title="Confirm every currently released quest is green">
        <p>Sort/filter the quest journal and confirm <strong>every currently released quest is green</strong>. This guide includes the quests released through September 2026: <strong>The Ides of Milk, The Red Reef, The Blood Moon Rises, Fallen From Grace, A Ruff Situation and Crab Quest</strong>, alongside the earlier quests and Grandmasters in 3.5. Learning the Ropes was completed on Tutorial Island. Finish any quests released since the guide was published before buying or wearing the cape; announced quests that are not yet playable can wait. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Quests/List" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Current quest list</a>.</p>
      </RouteStep>
      <RouteStep id="i36-cape" number="12" title="Buy the Quest point cape and hood — graduate">
        <p>With the journal all green, take <strong>99,000 coins</strong> to the <strong>Wise Old Man in Draynor Village</strong> and buy the <strong>Quest point cape and hood</strong>. When a new quest is released, complete it to wear and use the cape again. With this cape and the Fire Cape earned in 3.3, you have finished the Intermediate guide. <a href="https://oldschool.runescape.wiki/w/Quest_point_cape" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Cape ownership and purchase</a>.</p>
        <ExpandableNote title="Set aside 99,000 coins for the cape" label="Quest preparation">
          <p>Check that you have <strong>99,000 coins</strong> left after the final fights and any item reclaims. If short, return to <strong>Ardougne Knights with your Rogue outfit</strong>, banking and eating as needed. Stop when you can pay for the cape and immediate travel.</p>
        </ExpandableNote>
      </RouteStep>

      <section id="chapter-complete" class="completion-panel">
        <div class="section-label">Intermediate Guide Complete · choose your own direction</div>
        <h3>Quest Cape and Fire Cape earned. The route is yours now.</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Capes and combat:</strong> Quest point cape and hood, Fire Cape/Jad, Barrows gloves, Piety, dragon defender and Hallowed flail.</li>
          <li><strong>World and travel:</strong> Prifddinas, Vampyrium, fairy rings, Kingdom access, Drakan's medallion, Royal seed pod, Ring of shadows, house teleports and tablets, and the Ancient, Lunar and Arceuus spellbooks.</li>
          <li><strong>Quest experience:</strong> While Guthix Sleeps, Monkey Madness II, Theatre Entry, Dragon Slayer II, Desert Treasure II and The Blood Moon Rises, with every currently released quest complete.</li>
          <li><strong>Optional next goals:</strong> Bowfa/full crystal, Ava's assembler, Slayer helmet, whip, trident, zenytes, blowpipe, raid uniques, an ornate/max POH, diary cape or a high Combat Achievement tier.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section><div class="section-label">Where do I go now? · optional, unranked</div><h2>Pick a path because it sounds fun.</h2>
        <p>Choose whichever of these sounds enjoyable. <strong>Gauntlet/crystal</strong> can be a Bowfa project you return to in short sessions. <strong>Slayer</strong> can build toward black mask/helmet, whip, zenytes and higher levels. <strong>Vorkath</strong> can supply a head for Ava's assembler; <strong>Zulrah</strong> offers scales, a blowpipe and other uniques. Try <strong>raids</strong> with low-invocation Tombs of Amascut, already unlocked by Beneath Cursed Sands. Explore <strong>Vampyrium</strong> for bloodwood, skilling, Slayer and Maggot King. Or work on POH conveniences, diaries, Combat Achievements and teleports, or settle into relaxed skills, clues and a collection log. All of these are optional next adventures.</p>
      </section>
    </article>
    <aside class="sidebar right-rail"><ProgressTracker storageKey="rsag-intermediate-3-6" title="3.6 progress" /></aside>
    <IntermediatePager previousHref={`${base}intermediate/chapter-3-5/`} previousLabel="← 3.5" />
  </div>
